  "key_findings": [
    "Pooled 3-day metrics show flood report proportion rising from 22.67% (NORMAL) -> 54.06% (WATCH) -> 84.23% (HIGH_ALERT) -> 86.92% (CRITICAL_OVERFLOW), while NO_TELEMETRY reaches 88.07%.",
    "Important Confounding Finding: The 3-day pooled step pattern is heavily confounded by storm date (daily flood ratio jumps from 10.27% on Sep 24 -> 70.86% on Sep 25 -> 85.84% on Sep 26), and NO_TELEMETRY (88.07%) exceeds CRITICAL_OVERFLOW (86.92%) because missing telemetry slots occurred during peak storm hours on Sep 25-26. Therefore, pooled tiers reflect citywide pluvial storm timing rather than canal freeboard alone.",
    "Restricted to subdistricts near water stations (water_station_dist_km <= 2.0 km, 372 khwaeng-hours), CRITICAL_OVERFLOW has 82.78% flood reports (89 rows), HIGH_ALERT has 71.19% (74 rows), WATCH has 33.78% (96 rows), and NORMAL has 16.28% (71 rows)."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Temporal Confounding (Date/Storm Effect): Daily flood ratio jumps from 10.27% (Sep 24) to 70.86% (Sep 25) and 85.84% (Sep 26), and NO_TELEMETRY reaches 88.07%. Within-day comparisons show that during peak rain on Sep 25-26, flood complaint ratios are high across all citywide tiers due to widespread pluvial street drainage overload; canal freeboard alone does not causally explain the pooled step increase.",
    "Station Pairing Distance: Across all Bangkok subdistricts, distance to the nearest of the 8 water stations has median 5.26 km and max 20.33 km. Filtering to water_station_dist_km <= 2.0 km retains 372 rows out of 3972 to align with the near-station scope.",
    "Subdistrict Name Extraction via Regex: Extracting khwaeng/khet from Traffy text address yields 237 distinct (khwaeng, khet) pairs and 51 khet values (vs official 180 khwaengs and 50 khets) due to 'ไม่ระบุ' and spelling variations; post-checkpoint this will switch to ST_Contains spatial join with Issue #3 polygon boundaries.",
    "Sparse Hourly Grid & Representative Center: khwaeng_hourly contains only khwaeng-hours with >= 1 citizen report (hours with 0 reports are omitted), and khwaeng_centers averages report coordinates across all hours for each (khwaeng, khet).",
    "Station 10 (Khlong Phasi Charoen) exhibits a vertical datum mismatch (waterlevel -6.15m to -1.72m vs bank 1.42m) and is isolated under SUSPECT_DATUM (usable_for_freeboard=false)."
  ]
